# Run event watcher: type run events into the agent terminal that started the run

## What to build

The event-driven supervisor of KAN-92 in graph-manager (`apps/graph-manager`), spec `docs/prd/agent-supervisor.md` ("Run origins and the supervisor (KAN-92)" → `supervisor.ts`, "Event lines"). graph-manager polls the runs that have an origin terminal every 2 s, diffs each run's status and review step with what it saw last, and types one `[graph-manager] …` line into the origin terminal per event: `started`, `resumed`, `review`, `succeeded`, `failed`, `cancelled`. The `failed` line carries the workspace's Supervisor mode (`report` / `act`) and what the agent must do.

This slice adds `src/server/supervisor.ts` (`RunEventWatcher`, `eventLine`, the diff and the snapshot reader), the `supervisorPollMs` config field, and starts/stops the watcher in `buildApp`. It builds on code that already exists when you start:

- **`src/server/run-origins.ts`**: `class RunOrigins { set(wsId, runId, terminalId): void; get(wsId, runId): string | undefined; delete(wsId, runId): void; entries(): { wsId: string; runId: string; terminalId: string }[] }`, on the app context as `ctx.runOrigins` (`AppContext.runOrigins`; `BuildAppOptions.runOrigins` injects one in tests; `appWithLogin(configOverrides, { runOrigins })` in `test-helpers.ts` passes it through). Origins are recorded by the `graph-execution` shim, `POST /api/internal/run-origins`, `POST /api/internal/sandbox-runs` (with `terminalId`) and `POST /api/runs/:ws` (with `originTerminalId`).
- **`TerminalManager.typeWhenIdle(id, line): boolean`** in `src/server/terminals.ts`: queues the line, types it once the terminal has been quiet for 3 s (then `"\r"`), strips control characters, drops it for non-agent terminals or when the shell is in front. Returns `false` for an unknown or non-agent terminal. Never call `proc.write` yourself.
- **`src/server/store.ts`**: `export type SupervisorMode = "report" | "act"` and `export function supervisorModeOf(data: Data, wsId: string): SupervisorMode` (`"report"` when unset).

## Context: files to read before implementing

- `docs/prd/agent-supervisor.md` — Decisions rows "Event detection polls…", "Events are run-level only…", "The first time the watcher sees a run…", "The mode is written into the `failed` event's text…"; the `supervisor.ts` bullets and the exact "Event lines".
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/runs.ts`:
  - lines 20–43 `RunSummary` — `type: "run" | "suite"`, `id`, `status` (`running` | `applied` | `done` | `failed` | `aborted` | `interrupted` | `unknown`), `kind`, `failure?` (only for `failed`/`aborted`, e.g. `task 3 failed`, `validation failed`, `aborted at task 2`). **There is no `reviewStep` and no `tasksDir` in `RunSummary`** — read them from `state.json` (below).
  - lines 162–170 `readState(runDir)` (private) — the `stateSchema.safeParse(JSON.parse(readFile(<runDir>/state.json)))` pattern to copy.
  - lines 192–216 `failureOf`; lines 230–266 `summarize` — `status` becomes `"interrupted"` when state.json says `running` but no process (or container) drives the run any more.
  - lines 273–282 `listWorkspaceRuns(ws, prs?, dataDir?)` — pass `ctx.config.dataDir` so `failure` uses graph-manager's cached view of the run page.
  - line 518 `runDirOf(ws, runId)` = `<ws.path>/.graph-execution/<runId>`.
- `packages/graph-execution/src/state/state.ts` (lines 12–13 task statuses; 26 `runStatusSchema`; 41–60 `reviewStepSchema` / `reviewStateSchema`; 63–92 `stateSchema`: `tasksDir` is an **absolute** path, `tasks: Record<id, { status }>`, `review.phase`). Exported from `graph-execution/api` as `stateSchema` / `RunState`. **`state.review.phase` is `"validate"` from the moment the run is created** (`initialReviewState()`), so it can't tell on its own whether the review started. The review phase runs once every task is merged (`packages/graph-execution/src/review/phase.ts` line 90), so: *review step* = `state.review.phase` when `Object.keys(state.tasks).length > 0` and every task's status is `"merged"`, else `undefined`.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/viewcache.ts` (lines 1–60, and its `start()`/`stop()`) — the existing background poller started by `buildApp`; mirror its timer handling.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/app.ts` (lines 79–136) — where `ctx` is built and the `onClose` hooks are added (`viewCache.start()` at line 129, `app.addHook("onClose", async () => viewCache.stop())` at line 130).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/config.ts` (lines 8–24 `Config`) — add the optional field; `loadConfig` and `config.test.ts` need no change.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/workspaces.ts` (lines 57–70 `resolveWorkspace(root, id)`; it needs `<root>/<forge>/<owner>/<repo>/.git` to exist) and `type Workspace` (`{ id, path, … }`).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/test-helpers.ts` — `tempDir()`, `testConfig(dir, overrides)`, `appWithLogin(overrides, appOpts)`.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/runs.test.ts` (lines 1–60 setup; 140–180 "starts a fake run that … reaches applied") — the pattern for an end-to-end test with the real engine (`it.skipIf(!built)` with `const built = existsSync(defaultGraphExecutionBin())`, collecting started pids to kill in `afterEach`, `poll` helper).

## Patterns to follow

**Exact exports of `src/server/supervisor.ts`:**
```ts
export type RunEvent =
  | { kind: "started"; runId: string; tasksDir: string }
  | { kind: "resumed"; runId: string }
  | { kind: "review"; runId: string }
  | { kind: "succeeded"; runId: string; status: string }
  | { kind: "failed"; runId: string; failure: string }
  | { kind: "cancelled"; runId: string };

/** What the watcher knows about one run at one tick. */
export interface RunSnapshot {
  type: "run" | "suite";
  status: string;          // RunSummary.status
  failure?: string;        // RunSummary.failure
  tasksDir?: string;       // workspace-relative, "/" separators, from state.json
  reviewStep?: string;     // see reviewStepOf
}
export interface SeenRun { status: string; reviewStep?: string }

export function reviewStepOf(state: RunState): string | undefined;
export function eventLine(e: RunEvent, mode: SupervisorMode): string;
export function diffRun(runId: string, prev: SeenRun | undefined, cur: RunSnapshot): RunEvent[];
export async function snapshotRuns(ws: Workspace, runIds: ReadonlySet<string>, dataDir?: string): Promise<Map<string, RunSnapshot>>;

export interface RunEventWatcherOptions {
  /** Poll interval; default ctx.config.supervisorPollMs ?? 2000. */
  intervalMs?: number;
  /** Replaces snapshotRuns (tests). */
  snapshot?: (ws: Workspace, runIds: ReadonlySet<string>) => Promise<Map<string, RunSnapshot>>;
}
export class RunEventWatcher {
  constructor(ctx: Pick<AppContext, "config" | "store" | "terminals" | "runOrigins">, opts?: RunEventWatcherOptions);
  start(): void;
  stop(): Promise<void>;   // clears the timer, awaits a running tick
  tick(): Promise<void>;   // one poll; public for tests
}
```

**Event lines — exact text, one line, prefix `[graph-manager] `:**
```ts
const P = "[graph-manager] ";
started:   `${P}Run ${id} started (${tasksDir}).`
review:    `${P}Run ${id} entered review.`
succeeded: `${P}Run ${id} succeeded (${status}). Call get_artifacts to see what it wrote, open_run to show it.`
cancelled: `${P}Run ${id} was cancelled.`
resumed:   `${P}Run ${id} was resumed.`
failed:    `${P}Run ${id} failed: ${failure}. ` + (mode === "act"
  ? `Supervisor: act. Find the cause with get_run_log and get_node_output, fix it, commit, then call resume_run with runId ${id}.`
  : `Supervisor: report. Tell the user what failed and why (get_run_log, get_node_output); do not change code or rerun.`)
```
`failure` is `snapshot.failure` with newlines turned into spaces and trailing dots/spaces removed; when absent: `"interrupted"` for status `interrupted`, else `"failed"`. So a run whose summary says `task 3 failed` gives `[graph-manager] Run gm-1 failed: task 3 failed. Supervisor: report. Tell the user …`.

**Status → end event:** `applied`, `done` → `succeeded` (with that status); `failed`, `interrupted` → `failed`; `aborted` → `cancelled`; `running` / anything else → none.

**`diffRun(runId, prev, cur)`** — events in this order: `started`, `resumed`, `review`, then the end event:
```ts
const end = endOf(cur);                       // RunEvent | undefined from the table above
if (!prev) return [{ kind: "started", runId, tasksDir: cur.tasksDir ?? "unknown task folder" },
                   ...(cur.reviewStep ? [{ kind: "review", runId }] : []), ...(end ? [end] : [])];
const out: RunEvent[] = [];
if (["failed", "aborted", "interrupted"].includes(prev.status) && cur.status === "running") out.push({ kind: "resumed", runId });
if (!prev.reviewStep && cur.reviewStep) out.push({ kind: "review", runId });
if (end && endKind(prev.status) !== end.kind) out.push(end);   // failed → interrupted is not a second failure
return out;
```
(`endKind(status)` = the end event kind of a status, or undefined.) The first sight sends `started` and, for a run that already ended (fast fake runs end between two polls), its end event too. After an end event the run stays watched: a resume brings it back to `running` → `resumed`.

**Tick algorithm:**
```ts
if (this.ticking) return;                     // never overlap ticks
for each wsId in group(ctx.runOrigins.entries()):
  const ws = resolveWorkspace(ctx.config.workspacesDir, wsId);
  if (!ws) { delete its origins and seen entries; continue; }
  // An origin whose terminal no longer exists is deleted (spec).
  for each origin: if (!ctx.terminals.get(terminalId)) { ctx.runOrigins.delete(wsId, runId); seen.delete(key); }
  const snaps = await snapshot(ws, new Set(remaining runIds));
  for each remaining origin:
    const cur = snaps.get(runId);
    if (!cur || cur.status === "unknown") continue;            // folder or state.json not written yet: wait
    if (cur.type === "suite") { ctx.runOrigins.delete(wsId, runId); continue; }   // non-goal: suites
    // A hand-off between the launcher and the detached engine can look "interrupted" for one poll: believe it on the second.
    if (cur.status === "interrupted" && !this.interruptedOnce.has(key)) { this.interruptedOnce.add(key); continue; }
    if (cur.status !== "interrupted") this.interruptedOnce.delete(key);
    const events = diffRun(runId, seen.get(key), cur);
    seen.set(key, { status: cur.status, reviewStep: cur.reviewStep });
    const mode = supervisorModeOf(ctx.store.get(), wsId);    // read at event time
    for (const e of events) ctx.terminals.typeWhenIdle(terminalId, eventLine(e, mode));
```
Wrap each workspace in `try/catch` (log nothing, keep going): a tick must never throw out of the timer. `key` = `${wsId}/${runId}`. A `seen` entry is kept when `RunOrigins.set` replaces the terminal of a run (`resume_run` from another terminal): that terminal then gets `resumed`, not a second `started`.

**`snapshotRuns(ws, runIds, dataDir)`:** `const runs = await listWorkspaceRuns(ws, undefined, dataDir)`; for each summary whose `id` is in `runIds`: `{ type, status, failure }`, plus for `type === "run"` the parsed `<runDirOf(ws, id)>/state.json` (`stateSchema.safeParse`, ignore errors): `tasksDir: path.relative(ws.path, state.tasksDir).split(path.sep).join("/") || "."` and `reviewStep: reviewStepOf(state)`.

**Timer pattern:** `setInterval(() => void this.tick(), ms)` with `.unref()`; `stop()` does `clearInterval` and `await this.current` (the promise of a running tick).

**Wiring in `buildApp`** (after `ctx` is built, next to the view cache lines 129–130):
```ts
// Types run events into the agent terminal that started each run (docs/prd/agent-supervisor.md).
const watcher = new RunEventWatcher(ctx);
watcher.start();
app.addHook("onClose", async () => watcher.stop());
```

**Unit-test context** (no app needed):
```ts
const { dir, cleanup } = await tempDir();
const config = testConfig(dir);
await mkdir(path.join(config.workspacesDir, "github", "octo", "hello", ".git"), { recursive: true });
const store = await DataStore.open(config.dataDir);
const live = new Set(["t1"]);
const typeWhenIdle = vi.fn((_id: string, _line: string) => true);
const terminals = { get: (id: string) => (live.has(id) ? { id } : undefined), typeWhenIdle } as unknown as TerminalManager;
const runOrigins = new RunOrigins();
let snaps = new Map<string, RunSnapshot>();
const watcher = new RunEventWatcher({ config, store, terminals, runOrigins }, { snapshot: async () => snaps });
```

## Step-by-step tasks

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/config.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT**: in `Config`, `/** How often the run event watcher polls runs that have an origin terminal, in ms (docs/prd/agent-supervisor.md); default 2000. Tests set it lower. */ supervisorPollMs?: number;`. `loadConfig` stays as is (no env var).
- **VALIDATE**: `npm run typecheck`

### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/supervisor.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT**: everything in "Exact exports", "Event lines", "Status → end event", `diffRun`, the tick algorithm, `snapshotRuns` and the timer pattern. File header comment: what it does and a pointer to `docs/prd/agent-supervisor.md`.
- **IMPORTS**: `readFile` from `node:fs/promises`; `path` from `node:path`; `stateSchema, type RunState` from `graph-execution/api`; `type AppContext` from `./app.js`; `listWorkspaceRuns, runDirOf` from `./runs.js`; `supervisorModeOf, type SupervisorMode` from `./store.js`; `resolveWorkspace, type Workspace` from `./workspaces.js`. (`app.ts` will import `supervisor.ts`; a type-only import back from `./app.js` is fine.)
- **GOTCHA**: only runs with an origin are snapshotted (cost stays small). Don't import `RunOrigins` as a value just to build one; use `ctx.runOrigins`. `typeWhenIdle` already handles the quiet wait, so the watcher never waits itself. Lines contain no newline.
- **VALIDATE**: `npm run typecheck && npm run lint`

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/app.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT**: the wiring snippet, plus `import { RunEventWatcher } from "./supervisor.js";`. Additive edits only (other parallel tasks also add lines here).
- **VALIDATE**: `npm run typecheck`

### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/supervisor.test.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT**:
  - `eventLine`: each kind's exact text; `failed` in `report` and in `act` (the act line contains `Supervisor: act.` and `resume_run with runId gm-1`); a failure with a newline / trailing dot is cleaned; missing failure → `failed: interrupted.` / `failed: failed.`
  - `diffRun`: first sight of a running run → `[started]`; first sight of an applied run with review step → `[started, review, succeeded(applied)]`; running → running with review step newly set → `[review]`; running → failed → `[failed]`; failed → running → `[resumed]`; failed → interrupted → `[]`; running → aborted → `[cancelled]`; done → `succeeded(done)`.
  - `reviewStepOf`: undefined while a task is `running` or `failed` or when there are no tasks; `state.review.phase` once every task is `merged`.
  - `RunEventWatcher.tick()` with the unit-test context:
    1. no origins → `typeWhenIdle` not called and `snapshot` not called.
    2. origin `t1` for `gm-1` with `{ type: "run", status: "running", tasksDir: ".agents/tasks/x" }` → one call `("t1", "[graph-manager] Run gm-1 started (.agents/tasks/x).")`; a second tick with the same snapshot → no new call; then `status: "failed", failure: "task 2 failed"` → the report failure line; `store.update` setting `workspaceSettings[WS] = { supervisor: "act" }`, then resume (`running`) and fail again → `resumed`, then the `act` line with `resume_run with runId gm-1`.
    3. a run first seen already `applied` → `started` then `succeeded (applied)` in that order.
    4. the origin's terminal is gone (`live.delete("t1")`) → no call and `runOrigins.entries()` is empty after the tick.
    5. a suite snapshot → no call and the origin is deleted; a missing snapshot or `status: "unknown"` → no call, origin kept.
    6. `interrupted` is reported only on the second consecutive tick.
    7. an unknown workspace id in an origin → the origin is deleted.
  - `start()`/`stop()`: with `intervalMs: 20`, after ~100 ms the snapshot fake was called; after `await watcher.stop()` it is not called any more.
  - End to end (`it.skipIf(!built || process.platform === "win32")`, timeout 120 s, copy the setup of `routes/runs.test.ts` lines 1–60 and its pid cleanup): `const origins = new RunOrigins()`, `appWithLogin({ supervisorPollMs: 100 }, { runOrigins: origins })`, a workspace with the `diamond` fixture and `spec.md` committed, `vi.spyOn(TerminalManager.prototype, "typeWhenIdle").mockReturnValue(true)`, a plain terminal from `POST /api/terminals { workspaceId: WS }`, `POST /api/runs/:ws { tasksDir: "diamond", spec: "spec.md", provider: "fake", originTerminalId: <terminal id> }` → poll until the spy got the `succeeded` line; the spy's lines for that run are, in order, `[graph-manager] Run <id> started (diamond).`, `[graph-manager] Run <id> entered review.` and `[graph-manager] Run <id> succeeded (applied). Call get_artifacts to see what it wrote, open_run to show it.` (The fake run is fast: the review line may only be produced together with the end event on first sight; the order still holds.) Close the run page (`POST <viewUrl>close`) before cleanup as `runs.test.ts` does.
- **PATTERN**: `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/runs.test.ts:140-180`.
- **VALIDATE**: `npm test -w graph-manager -- src/server/supervisor.test.ts`

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] `buildApp` starts a `RunEventWatcher` that polls every `config.supervisorPollMs ?? 2000` ms and stops on `app.close()`.
- [ ] Only runs with an origin are watched; per run the events come in the order `started`, `resumed`, `review`, then `succeeded` / `failed` / `cancelled`; the first sight sends `started` and the end event of an already-ended run.
- [ ] The lines are exactly the spec's (see "Event lines"), sent with `ctx.terminals.typeWhenIdle(<origin terminal>, line)`; the failure line ends with the `report` text by default and with `Supervisor: act. … then call resume_run with runId <id>.` when the workspace's Supervisor is `act`.
- [ ] Status mapping: `applied`/`done` → succeeded, `failed`/`interrupted` → failed (no duplicate for failed → interrupted; `interrupted` believed on the second tick), `aborted` → cancelled, back to `running` from failed/aborted/interrupted → resumed; `review` when every task is merged (review step from `state.json`).
- [ ] An origin whose terminal no longer exists, whose workspace is gone, or that is a suite is deleted; a run whose folder/state isn't there yet is waited for.
- [ ] Tests pass: `npm test -w graph-manager -- src/server/supervisor.test.ts`

## Validation commands

```bash
# from the repo root
npm run typecheck && npm run lint
npm test -w graph-manager -- src/server/supervisor.test.ts
npm test -w graph-manager
```
